<title>GERMANY: Air France's German cargo not hit by trucker strike.</title>
<headline>Air France's German cargo not hit by trucker strike.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France said its Germany cargo operations have been unaffected by the French truckers strike.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not been affected by the strikes,&quot; Air France Cargo director for Germany, Helmut Scherret, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The truckers are more interested in blocking the main routes to the south and the eastbound route (via Saarbruecken) has been clear,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Air France Cargo transports most of its ex-Germany cargo by truck to its Paris hub, with a substantial proportion crossing the border at Saarbruecken.</p>
<p>French unions said 50,000 truck drivers had blocked roads over the last four days in protest actions including the Franco-German border at Strasburg. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
